Shims for running unmodified CUA-World task scripts as an unprivileged user (rootless Singularity container).
They are first on PATH inside the image.  Every call is logged to /tmp/ves-shim.log.

  sudo       drops its options and runs the command as the current user
  su         `su - ga -c CMD` runs CMD in a login shell (as the current user, cwd $HOME = /home/ga)
  apt-get    packages are installed in the image; checks that the requested ones are present, always succeeds
  apt        same as apt-get
  chown      runs the real chown, ignores failures (other users' ids are not mapped)
  chgrp      same
  pip, pip3  ignored (the Python packages the tasks need are installed in the image)
  systemctl, service   ignored
